# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# setup: benchpart
# board: only
# One PART of a suite, run on its own.
#
# A suite is a set of checks and sometimes only one of them is the
# question being asked.  The bench can already run one alone; what this
# adds is somewhere to see them and pick, so the list opens to show a
# suite's own parts and running takes whichever row was chosen.
wait 60
click 980 30
wait 10
menu-pick Applications
wait 10
menu-pick Bench
wait 250
expect-title Bench
note the list holds only what a board on THIS desk can answer, so the
note row counted to here is the same row every time -- the first Down
note takes the top row, so one more than its number gets there
click-window Bench
wait 8
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
key Down
wait 3
wait 8
note opening a suite shows its own parts, each one runnable alone
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Show the parts of link-console
menu-pick Show the parts of link-console
wait 12
click-window Bench
wait 8
key Down
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Run on tiku
note the results window is made only when the bench has said something,
note and a part that did not exist would make the bench say nothing at all
wait 900
expect-title Results
note and the board is the shell's again afterwards
wait 400
expect-read /devices/tiku/sys/device/name tiku
quit
